SUMMARY: Newcomer Employment & Entrepreneurship Skills Hub (NEESH)
DESCRIPTION:Newcomer Employment & Entrepreneurship Skills Hub (NEESH) is 
 now accepting applications (starting August 11) for autumn cohorts.\n\nA 
 job can change your future. The right connections can change everything. 
 Looking for work in a new country can be overwhelming\, but you don't hav
 e to do it alone.\n\nThis free program is offered by Scadding Court Commu
 nity Centre in partnership with the Diversity Institute at Toronto Metrop
 olitan University (TMU). It is funded by the federal government.\n\nStart
 s October 3rd\, 2026\n\nEligibility: Newcomers with PR or Convention Refu
 gee status\, residing in the GTA\n\nFormat:\n\n  * 6-weeks hybrid trainin
 g at TMU\n  * + childcare and TTC cards\n  * 1:1\, specialized career sup
 ports\, coaching\, mock interviews\, resume reviews\, placement opportuni
 ties\, networking\, and mentorship\n  * wrap-around supports related to: 
 settlement\, career\, family\, GBV support and mental health referrals\n\
 nCertificates are granted upon completion.\n\nApplication: https://ryerso
 ntrsm.ca1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_0HetxesTdTc8USO?%20%5Bryersontrsm.ca1
 .qualtrics.com%5D%20%5Bryersontrsm.ca1.qualtrics.com%5D [ryersontrsm.ca1.
 qualtrics.com] https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ryersontrsm.ca1.qualtr
 ics.com/jfe/form/SV_0HetxesTdTc8USO?*20*5Bryersontrsm.ca1.qualtrics.com*5
 D*20*5Bryersontrsm.ca1.qualtrics.com*5D__\;JSUlJSUl!!KW-VMAODMJ4p!27kMK89
 HisKl-DCL6_WCxmY5K5zX3xph2uA9ceYcpLfPEQXwBGXY_qbHDz9F1m9bZ7g1uTZFvonNvY-v
 LM_V$\n\nFunded by Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada (IRCC).
