URL:https://tockify.com/st.lawrence.na/detail/350/1794443400000
SUMMARY: 'Hunger' at the Alumnae Theatre (Nov 11 to Nov 22)
DESCRIPTION:ALUMNAE THEATRE OPENS ALL-CANADIAN\, ALL-FEMALE PLAYWRIGHT SE
 ASON WITH MEGHAN GREELEY’S HUNGER\n\nAlumnae Theatre is proud to launch i
 ts 2026/2027 season\, centred around the theme Stories of Survival\, with
  Newfoundland playwright Meghan Greeley’s riveting drama\, Hunger. Direct
 ed by Sarini Kumarasinghe and produced by Kimberley Ann Croscup\, the pro
 duction runs from November 11 to November 22\, 2026\, in the Studio Theat
 re.\n\nHunger marks the opening production in a milestone season for Alum
 nae Theatre\, featuring a lineup written entirely by Canadian female play
 wrights.\n\nSet in an isolated farmhouse during an unspecified period of 
 war\, Hunger explores survival\, currency\, and the fragile nature of mor
 ality. In the midst of a violent conflict\, Johanna and Max attempt an ac
 t of heroics by hiding three refugees in a tiny alcove behind their walls
 . As space and food dwindle and the war outside reaches a deafening clima
 x\, the couple and their secret guests are pushed to their absolute limit
 s.\n\nFirst premiered by Newfoundland’s White Rooster Theatre in 2019 bef
 ore embarking on a provincial tour\, Greeley’s play earned widespread cri
 tical acclaim upon its publication by Breakwater Books\, where it was nam
 ed a finalist for the prestigious BMO Winterset Award. Praised by literar
 y reviewers for its "askew dialogue and cutaway violence" reminiscent of 
 the haunting\, surrealist works of Caryl Churchill\, Hunger delivers a te
 nse\, dark examination of human nature under extreme duress.\n\n"We’re th
 rilled to begin our season with a play that so fiercely challenges our un
 derstanding of human endurance and compassion\," says the production team
 . "Greeley's voice sets a fitting tone for a season dedicated to extraord
 inary stories of survival written by some of Canada’s most compelling fem
 ale theatre artists."\n\nThe cast is led by Yolande Williams and Ryan Gie
 sen (as Johanna and Max) with Kimberly Van Vo\, Arya Ashoori\, and Irene 
 Kalogridis (as Rivka\, Isaac\, and Helen) filling out this ensemble of st
 riking local talent.\n\nPRODUCTION INFORMATION:\n\n  * Hunger by Meghan G
 reeley\n  * Directed by Sarini Kumarasinghe\n  * Produced by Kimberley An
 n Croscup\n  * Location: Studio Theatre\, Alumnae Theatre (70 Berkeley St
 reet\, Toronto)\n  * Tickets and information: alumnaetheatre.com/hunger h
 ttp://alumnaetheatre.com/hunger\n\nCast\n\n  * Joanna: Yolande Williams\n
   * Max: Ryan Giesen\n  * Rivka: Kimberly Van Vo\n  * Isaac: Arya Ashoori
 \n  * Helen: Irene Kalogridis\n\nProduction Team\n\n  * Stage Manager: Lu
 ísa Teixeira\n  * Sound Designer: Ian Ottis Goff\n  * Lighting Designer:
  Sephora N'Kosi\n  * Set Designer: Douglas Tiller\n  * Costume Designer: 
 Gabe Woo\n  * Props Designer: Lori Delorme\n  * Intimacy Director: Jes Wa
 reing\n\nTicket and Economically Accessible Theatre Information\n\n  * Ge
 neral admission tickets are available for purchase.\n  * Thrifty Thursday
  - Tickets on the first Thursday of the run are only $10\n  * Second Wedn
 esday performance: Buy One Get One Free (BOGO).\n  * Sunday performances:
  Pay-What-You-Wish.\n\nPerformance Schedule\n\n  * Wednesday\, November 1
 1\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Thursday\, November 12\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Friday
 \, November 13\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 - 2:00P
 M\n  * Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Sunday\, November 15\,
  2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Wednesday\, November 18\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Thursday
 \, November 19\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Friday\, November 20\, 2026 - 7:30PM\
 n  * Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 -2:00PM\n  * Saturday\, November 21\, 
 2026 - 7:30PM\n  * Sunday\, November 22\, 2026 - 7:30PM\n\n––\n\nMedia Co
 ntact: Chelsea Lefaivre [marketing@alumnaetheatre.com mailto:marketing@al
 umnaetheatre.com ]\n\n––\n\nFounded in 1918\, Alumnae Theatre is the olde
 st women-run theatre company in North America and Canada’s longest runnin
 g theatre group. The Company is a women-led theatre company dedicated to 
 presenting compelling theatre\, incubating new works and nurturing the vo
 ices of women. A home for theatre-makers\, storytellers\, innovators and 
 collaboration.
